{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For he is a son of old age.</b> Its plain sense: he begot him when he was ninety-one years old. Likewise his brother Benjamin was called \"a child of old age\" (Genesis 44:20), and after these two no other was born to him." "<b>Pasim.</b> An embroidered tunic." "<b>Pasim.</b> Like פַס יְדָא (Daniel 5:5) in the Aramaic tongue."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:12.879667118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}